# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort spec=priest:discipline
# style=wander view=820x1180,touch save=carried.
#
# wander has never been run on a battleground before (checked sessions.jsonl:
# every prior battleground cell used dodge/flee/melee/good/auto/mash). It
# presses a random ability slot round-robin and picks a new random heading
# every twelve steps -- unlike flee/dodge it does not retreat, unlike
# good/melee it does not walk at anything on purpose. direction.md's #7 line
# says a body that presses nothing (flee/dodge) finishes healthy while the
# team still loses, and a body that presses something real (good) dies in a
# 9-16s band because the whole party spawns clustered on the enemy boss-actor
# and good's beeline walks straight into it. wander has no beeline at all, so
# it's the open middle case: does it die the way good does (nothing to do
# with steering-at-a-target, since wander doesn't steer at one) or survive
# the way flee/dodge do (nothing to do with retreating, since wander doesn't
# retreat either)? First healer under this style on any battleground too.
# carried save is known-fresh-in-disguise per #273 (still open), so nothing
# here relies on anything actually carrying.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:escort
targets
shot escort-picked

tap class:priest:discipline
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play wander 90
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
